{"version":"1","id":"laraveldaily","handle":"laraveldaily","name":"Laravel Daily","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--vzdgNGfl--/f_auto/v1725044498/logos/laraveldaily","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.98,"y":3.7328,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":478,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-07T06:08:03.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-06-24T05:00:18.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.011506,"listicle_ratio":0.064854,"question_ratio":0.069038,"avg_read_time":7.554393,"summary_length_avg":455.501119,"title_length_avg":53.07113,"title_length_var":121.292012,"tag_entropy":2.769375,"tag_diversity":0.221757,"top_tag_share":0.046025,"avg_upvotes":4.311715,"median_upvotes":2.0,"avg_comments":0.125523,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.029583,"zero_engagement_share":0.267782,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":5.445239,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.098851},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.7941,-0.2794],"cadence_depth":[8.3529,3.2794],"hype_variety":[1.9706,-4.2059],"title_style":[7.3824,8.7941]},"top_tags":[["laravel",421],["php",311],["webdev",246],["database",46],["ai",34],["authentication",23],["open-source",22],["career",21]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["3 Tools to Draw/Manage Database Schema","5 essential tips from senior developers for juniors","4 tips to boost developer productivity"],"outlier":["Laravel boost adds six new features including improved AI guidelines and editor support"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"OhR3yPl2Q","title":"NEW Package Laravel Brain: Visualize your Codebase to Understand It Better","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ex7pc-5X9R8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-package-laravel-brain-visualize-your-codebase-to-understand-it-better-ohr3ypl2q","summary":"Laravel Brain is a new open-source package for Laravel that scans your codebase and generates interactive visual diagrams of routes, controllers, methods, queries, and service calls. It helps developers quickly understand unfamiliar projects by showing method flow, complexity, and relationships between components. The package supports multiple graph layouts, PNG/Mermaid export, AI context export for coding agents, and has early support for Filament PHP. A hands-on demo walks through using it on two real projects, highlighting where it adds value for larger, more complex codebases.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ex7pc-5X9R8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T06:08:03.000Z"},{"id":"YACltntY5","title":"I Spent a Month on Upwork. My Conclusions and Advice for Devs.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GXnGZsucKGI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-spent-a-month-on-upwork-my-conclusions-and-advice-for-devs--yacltnty5","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/GXnGZsucKGI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T08:16:03.000Z"},{"id":"DYJcL1T6G","title":"New Laravel Package Trace-Replay: Another Local Debugger but... Better?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mrTiSJp2nOI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-laravel-package-trace-replay-another-local-debugger-but-better--dyjcl1t6g","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/mrTiSJp2nOI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T05:00:43.000Z"},{"id":"Odfyv3EMa","title":"New Laravel Package AI GEO: Generate Schema for ChatGPT","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v2Ii-j624kQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-laravel-package-ai-geo-generate-schema-for-chatgpt-odfyv3ema","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/v2Ii-j624kQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-30T06:03:00.000Z"},{"id":"weXHtl0pW","title":"Next.js Fundamentals for Laravel Developers (New Course!)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-sq7SjXAyW0","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/next-js-fundamentals-for-laravel-developers-new-course--wexhtl0pw","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/-sq7SjXAyW0/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29T05:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"oOSRV2iCx","title":"New Package: Laravel Fluent Validation - Performance Demo (Before/After)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WClB1fCTc98","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-package-laravel-fluent-validation---performance-demo-before-after--oosrv2icx","summary":"A demonstration of the Laravel Fluent Validation package, which offers a chainable, IDE-autocomplete-friendly syntax for Laravel validation rules. Beyond syntax improvements, the package optimizes database queries for large array validation by batching exists/unique rule checks \u2014 reducing 1000+ queries down to 2 in a benchmark of 500 products with 5 variants each, cutting response time from ~1 second to ~85ms. The video walks through before/after comparisons using two form request classes and covers additional features like Livewire/Filament integration, Rector migration support, and nested array validation with each/children helpers.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WClB1fCTc98/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T06:33:35.000Z"},{"id":"Uc0WpKO0x","title":"Why attending live developer events can boost your career","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=95jO14xHIOA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/one-lifehack-that-will-boost-your-dev-career-uc0wpko0x","summary":"Attending live developer events \u2014 conferences, meetups, or even ones you organize yourself \u2014 is one of the most underrated career moves for developers. Real-life interactions build trust faster than any online engagement, and trust is the key factor behind hiring decisions and collaborations. Examples from the Laravel community show that many job offers, partnerships, and joint projects trace back to in-person conversations at events like Laracon. Even small local meetups of 5\u201320 people can open unexpected doors. The advice: show up, be visible, talk to people, and if no local meetup exists, start one.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/95jO14xHIOA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-25T07:00:07.000Z"},{"id":"i4pljBgUO","title":"NEW in Laravel 13.6: Debounced Queue Jobs","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PB2_XykYilg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-in-laravel-13-6-debounced-queue-jobs-i4pljbguo","summary":"Laravel 13.6 introduces debounced queue jobs, a new feature that ensures only the last dispatch of a repeated job within a time window actually executes. This is useful for bulk operations where multiple events trigger the same expensive job \u2014 for example, recalculating a customer's lifetime value when 10 orders are updated at once. Without debouncing, 10 separate jobs run sequentially (taking ~20 seconds); with debouncing set to 10 seconds, only the final job executes (~2 seconds total). The feature supports customization like max wait time and cache configuration, and is compared to the existing `shouldBeUnique` approach in the official pull request.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/PB2_XykYilg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-22T11:47:46.000Z"},{"id":"q7YgAHNFO","title":"How I Deployed Laravel API with Laravel Forge","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gel-35Wtw-E","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-i-deployed-laravel-api-with-laravel-forge-q7ygahnfo","summary":"A walkthrough of deploying a Laravel API project using Laravel Forge, covering site creation from a GitHub repository, customizing the deployment script (removing unneeded npm, migrations, and storage link steps), managing environment variables, enabling automatic deployments with zero-downtime, and exporting OpenAPI documentation for submission to RapidAPI.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/gel-35Wtw-E/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-21T05:46:30.000Z"},{"id":"UpjAcUyEy","title":"Laravel API for RapidAPI: Real Upwork Job using Codex CLI","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UG_RxFclFIM","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/laravel-api-for-rapidapi-real-upwork-job-using-codex-cli-upjacuyey","summary":"A walkthrough of building a text cleaner Laravel API and publishing it to RapidAPI, using Codex CLI as an AI assistant. Covers API versioning with a V1 prefix, adding a health check endpoint, generating OpenAPI documentation with the Scramble package, and uploading the JSON spec to RapidAPI. The video demonstrates a practical workflow where Codex handles boilerplate tasks like adding doc blocks and refactoring tests while the developer reviews and approves changes.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UG_RxFclFIM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-20T07:53:28.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["theburningmonk","steveklabnik","deno","dreamsofcode","nodeland"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","hamelhusain","xai","hwchase17","sama"],"similar":[{"id":"theburningmonk","handle":"theburningmonk","name":"theburningmonk.com","is_squad":false,"x":-4.918,"y":3.6149,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":74,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/07b15094e5264cbc974631fd43894816","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.503038,"median_upvotes":2.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.006757,"avg_read_time":6.418919,"tag_diversity":0.608108},"top_tags_preview":[["serverless",65],["aws",64],["aws-lambda",31]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[7.1471,1.3088],"cadence_depth":[-1.9853,1.1176],"hype_variety":[-0.3382,-5.2647],"title_style":[9.6029,4.0735]}},{"id":"steveklabnik","handle":"steveklabnik","name":"Steve Klabnik","is_squad":false,"x":-4.8262,"y":3.6828,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":22,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/7610ab034d884941bc56294e0912125b","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.158254,"median_upvotes":1.0,"